  "id": "COMPOUND:34435 - PROTEIN:4022",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Gloeosteretriol appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the Proteasome subunit alpha type-7. The first pathway links Ent-Gloeosteretriol to DMS-53, which is targeted by Gerontoisoflavone A, and Gerontoisoflavone A is shown to target the Proteasome subunit alpha type-7. In another pathway, Ent-Gloeosteretriol is directly linked to Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which in turn targets the same subunit. A third pathway connects Ent-Gloeosteretriol to Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, which is targeted by Oblonganoside C, also leading to the Proteasome subunit alpha type-7. These findings suggest that Ent-Gloeosteretriol may act through various molecular mechanisms, potentially modulating the proteasome pathway through different intermediaries. The evidence supports a broader role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol in influencing proteasome function, though the exact mechanism by which it interacts with the subunit remains to be fully elucidated.",
